(Stage 1e1 review — nesting combined with the other tags, and a MUTUAL
 cycle rather than the self-cycle of test 171. A nested list holding a
 float exercises PRINT_FLOAT inside the recursive frame; a two-list cycle
 must hit the same depth bound and set the error flag; an empty child must
 render as [] rather than being skipped.)

a list called "inner" is [1.5, "s", yes].
a list called "outer" is [].
append 7 to outer.
append inner to outer.
append 2.5 to outer.
print outer.
If element 2 of outer is a list, print "elem2 is list".
Otherwise print "elem2 not list".

a list called "empty_child" is [].
a list called "holder" is [].
append empty_child to holder.
print holder.

a list called "aa" is [].
a list called "bb" is [].
append aa to bb.
append bb to aa.
print aa.
on error print "cycle-flagged".
